# The instrument each composition is filed under, rendered as one string. One row per citation.
#
# A declared mapping must render something
#   `composition_citation` names `documentation` on diagrams/domain_objects.sqlc. No count can see
#   whether it renders, because element kinds are not one to one: `documentation` is also spent by
#   the pools and the lanes, so its count can be exact while this table's share of it is zero. A
#   mapping declared and never rendered can hide exactly there, and diagrams/ungoverned.sqlc exists
#   for that.
#
# It loses the structure, not the words
#   The columns settle it: `pm.composition_citation` is `(taxonomy, instrument, clause, version)`,
#   four typed fields, not free prose. A `documentation` element carries all four, as one string, so
#   a reader can read the citation and a tool cannot resolve it. That is narrower than losing
#   everything, and worth being exact about, because the two states need different repairs.
#
# The open question is the schema's
#   Not the diagram's. `(composition, seq)` is a bare position in the document, where both sibling
#   children of a composition carry a regime handle, and `merge-group-composition` cites one
#   instrument while crossing several regime boundaries. The emission cannot fix that and must not
#   cover it up.
-- asrt:Composition/asrt:citation, flattened to the one string a documentation element can hold.
SELECT c.composition,
       c.instrument
         || coalesce(' clause ' || c.clause, '')
         || coalesce(' (' || c.version || ')', '')
         || ' under ' || c.taxonomy AS cited
FROM (
    :compose(composition/citations.sqlc)
) c
